You have Azure Machine Learning workspaces for development, staging, and production.

The workspaces are deployed and updated only by using the same Bicep module and environment-specific parameter files.

You have training jobs in each workspace that download packages from an approved external package repository. The repository is referenced by DNS name and is not available through a private endpoint.

You plan to enforce a new outbound network baseline for all three workspaces.

You need to configure the Bicep module. The solution must meet the following requirements:

• Prevent unrestricted internet egress from managed compute.
• Allow training jobs to reach the approved package repository.
• Use the existing parameter for the repository destination.

How should you complete the Bicep file? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.

NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.

```bicep
param workspaceName string
param location string = resourceGroup().location
param approvedRepository string

resource workspace 'Microsoft.MachineLearningServices/workspaces@2025-09-01' = {
  name: workspaceName
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Basic'
  }
  properties: {
    managedNetwork: {
      isolationMode: [BLANK 1]
    }
  }
}

resource outboundRule 'Microsoft.MachineLearningServices/workspaces/outboundRules@2025-09-01' = {
  name: 'approvedRepository'
  parent: workspace
  properties: {
    category: 'UserDefined'
    destination: approvedRepository
    type: [BLANK 2]
  }
}
```
